SUMMARY
New table public.loan_statements: id PK, property_id, financial_year_end,
interest_paid, lender, account_ref, period_start/end, storage_path,
extracted jsonb, confidence, confirmed_at, timestamps.

FILES
- supabase/migrations/055_loan_statements.sql (new)
- lib/supabase/database.types.ts - LoanStatement row type + Tables entry

DESIGN DECISIONS
- Per statement, not per property. property_loans is PK'd on property_id
  (one loan per property), but a real property can carry several loan
  accounts. account_ref distinguishes them; the FY deduction is the sum.
- Partial unique index on (property_id, financial_year_end, account_ref)
  WHERE account_ref IS NOT NULL. Stops duplicate statements for an
  identified account without constraining unidentified single loans.
- confirmed_at gates claimability, mirroring staged_receipts: AI proposes,
  a human confirms. extracted + confidence are retained so a confirmed
  figure can always be compared against what the model actually read.
- jsonb typed as Record<string, unknown> to match the existing convention
  in this file (property_enrichment, staged_receipts).

FILE-BEARING TABLE
storage_path targets the property-files bucket. Reusing that bucket avoids
new storage RLS policies, and it is invisible in the Files UI because that
list is driven by property_files rows, not by bucket contents. The column
must still be added to user_storage_objects() and
property_storage_objects() - handled in the deletion-invariants task.

